            <ArticleTitle>A case of combined soft tissue and intraosseous venous malformation of the thumb treated with sclerotherapy using a bone marrow aspiration needle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/23320885.2014.1003561</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vascular malformations of bone are complex lesions that can cause deformity and pain. A combined soft tissue and intraosseous venous malformation of the left thumb in a girl was treated with two sessions of ethanol sclerotherapy using a bone marrow aspiration needle under fluoroscopic guidance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
